# `atomics_e2e` -- compiler-level atomics executed on the Tiny machine (TESTCASES-050).
#
# Layer split (user ruling A, 2026-11-15): the *instruction* layer (lr/sc RMW
# synthesis order) is carried by tests/inst/00-isa-design/atomic_rmw.S
# (m13-testcases-049).  The *compiler* layer -- the value semantics of the
# `__atomic_*` builtins and the C11 `<stdatomic.h>` wrappers -- is what this
# guest program runs for real: lr/sc retry loops on file-scope objects, plus the
# sub-word read-modify-write neighbour guard.
#
# What is asserted, and where:
#   * runtime value semantics (old value returned, memory updated, CAS failure
#     leaves memory untouched, expected updated) -> the QEMU guest exit code;
#     0 = all 20 checks pass, N = check N failed (see atomics_e2e.c).  The
#     freestanding e2e programs have no stdio, so the code IS the report
#     (same shape as fma_e2e.c).
#   * lowering shape (one lr/sc pair per width, no libatomic/`__sync_*`
#     out-of-line call, seq_cst fence present) -> the FileCheck/grep lines.
#
# NOT asserted here (registered as a GAP in tests/inst/MIGRATION.md, ISS-440 /
# ISS-443): contention behaviour (ABA, mutual-exclusion counters, `a_barrier`
# observables) and the *strength* of the emitted `fence` ordering.  Both need a
# multi-hart machine; a single-hart guest cannot distinguish relaxed from
# seq_cst.  The operand below is therefore pinned as "what the backend emits",
# not as "sufficient ordering".
#
# RUN: %clang -target dadao-unknown-elf -nostdlib -O2 -S %e2e_dir/atomics_e2e.c -o %t.s
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ASM < %t.s
# RUN: %not grep -q '__atomic' %t.s
# RUN: %not grep -q '__sync' %t.s
# RUN: %clang -target dadao-unknown-elf -nostdlib -O2 -c %e2e_dir/atomics_e2e.c -o %t.o
# RUN: %llvm_mc --triple=dadao-unknown-elf -filetype=obj %crt0 -o %t.crt0.o
# RUN: %ld -T %linker_script %t.crt0.o %t.o -o %t.elf
# RUN: timeout 30 %qemu -machine dadao-tiny,bootrom-image=%bootrom -kernel %t.elf -semihosting-config enable=on,target=native -display none -nographic

# seq_cst RMW: a fence before the lr/sc loop (order strength = GAP, shape = pinned).
# ASM: fence cfx_umon, 4095
# 4-byte (`t`) RMW: the 5 fetch_* ops, both 4-byte exchanges and the 4-byte CAS.
# ASM: lr.t.an rd{{[0-9]+}}, [rb{{[0-9]+}}]
# ASM: sc.t.ar rd{{[0-9]+}}, rd{{[0-9]+}}, [rb{{[0-9]+}}]
# 8-byte (`o`) RMW: 64-bit fetch_add / exchange / compare_exchange.
# ASM: lr.o.an rd{{[0-9]+}}, [rb{{[0-9]+}}]
# ASM: sc.o.ar rd{{[0-9]+}}, rd{{[0-9]+}}, [rb{{[0-9]+}}]
# 1-/2-byte narrow RMW: full-width lr/sc + masking, neighbours preserved.
# ASM: lr.b.an rd{{[0-9]+}}, [rb{{[0-9]+}}]
# ASM: sc.b.ar rd{{[0-9]+}}, rd{{[0-9]+}}, [rb{{[0-9]+}}]
# ASM: lr.w.an rd{{[0-9]+}}, [rb{{[0-9]+}}]
# ASM: sc.w.ar rd{{[0-9]+}}, rd{{[0-9]+}}, [rb{{[0-9]+}}]
